# Realm-scoped chatter, one realm per block: realm pride and rivalry, races, classes, culture, home zones and
# dungeons, and general frontier talk. Places are only that realm's (or Darkness Falls and the battlegrounds),
# always with @about place or a near:/at:/going: need. New writing for Offline DAoC (see docs/bot-voices).

# =====================================================================================================
# ALBION
# =====================================================================================================

# ---------------- Albion: pride, rivalry, races, culture ----------------
@kind ambient
@topic realm_pride
@realm alb
@who *
[say what you will|honestly|call me biased], albion [still has|has] the best [armor|healers|casters] in the game
[hibs|mids] [keep|never stop] [complaining|crying] about our [clerics|wizards|armsmen], must be doing something right
[heh, |]nothing in the game beats a line of [armsmen|paladins] [holding a door|standing shoulder to shoulder]
[a hib|some hib] told me [lurikeens|elves] are [fearsome|dangerous|scary] up close, [i laughed|i almost believed him|sure they are]
[mids|midgard folk] think [trolls|their trolls] are [subtle|sneaky|quiet], i [heard|smelled] one from three hills away
highlanders yelling in a group is my favorite sound in the realm
avalons always look like they are about to correct your spelling
inconnu give me the shivers, glad they picked our side
saracens are the best looking race in any realm, no further questions
briton is the plain choice and it never lets you down
[i was raised on|i grew up on|nothing beats] [old|] king arthur stories, [this realm feels like home|no other realm ever made sense to me]
long live the king, wherever he wandered off to
albion was here first and the other two know it
[our|albion] music is all lutes and [flutes|pipes], not [drums and shouting|goat horns|whatever the mids call singing]
minstrels are basically the realm's town criers with a lute
ever notice albion guards look like they could actually fight
reavers are what happens when the church loses track of a knight
necromancers creep me out but i want one in every group
cabalist pets are uglier than anything a hib could grow
theurgist pets everywhere, the whole realm sounds like a beehive
sorcerers put the whole room to sleep and call it teamwork
mercenaries are just armsmen who skipped the sermons
paladin chants could put a baby to sleep, but they keep us standing
scouts are the realm's eyes and most of its complaints
every infiltrator swears he fights fair. i have my doubts
[mids|the mids] [smell like|always smell of] [wet dog|old mead|fish] and [nobody|not one of them] has [mentioned it|noticed]
[hibs|hibernians] [dye|paint] everything [purple|bright green|pink], [and call it stealth|then wonder why we spot them|its a wonder they sneak at all]
a kobold asked me for directions once. then he stabbed me. typical midgard
a friar with a quarterstaff is the most albion thing there is
i trust a cleric with a mace over any druid with a twig
the church of albion has rules for everything, even for fun
albion breeds stubborn people, its all the rain
[sometimes|now and then] i stop [on a hill|on the road] just to look at [the countryside|the green hills|the old castles]
[anyone else think|does anyone else think] albion has the [best|prettiest] [castles|countryside] of the three realms?
what do you think makes albion better than the other two?
albs argue about everything, then line up behind the same banner
nobody does honor like albion. nobody does paperwork like albion either
there is a guild for everything in albion, probably a guild for guilds too
the defenders of albion take their job seriously, try telling a joke near one
the guild of shadows is not half as secret as it thinks
the academy smells like old books and singed eyebrows
i like how albion feels old, like the stones remember things
a hot stew in a tavern after a long hunt, that is albion
[the mids eat raw fish|mids eat anything that moves], [the hibs eat flowers|hibs live on berries], we eat proper food
albion has the best castles, the other realms have the best excuses
[a good|any proper] alb [knows|remembers] that [a sword is only as good as the arm behind it|the realm comes first|you never leave a cleric behind]
[i like|nothing beats] the sound of [church bells|a minstrel tuning up] in an albion village
the other realms have magic, we have magic and manners
saracens and highlanders in the same group, the arguments never end
[my|my old] [mentor|guildmaster] said a true alb never [runs|leaves a friend behind], [then he ran|i think about that a lot|he was mostly right]
the realm feels bigger every year, or i walk slower
@invites joke
a hib, a mid and an alb walk into a keep. only the alb walks out
how many mids does it take to light a torch? none, the troll already ate it
why did the lurikeen cross the road? he couldnt see over the hedge
[i tried to|once i tried to] teach a [troll|kobold] to [read|use a fork|bow], [it did not go well|we are both still confused|i gave up after an hour]
heard the hibs train their pets to cry when an alb walks by
[mids|the mids] say we wear too much armor. [they say it from the floor|they say that until they hit it|funny how they never say it twice]
albion knights never bow to a hib, mostly because we cant find them
@invites boast
albion plate shines brighter than anything a mid ever hammered
[proud|happy] to be an alb, [best realm|best people|best ale] in the land and [nobody can tell me otherwise|i will hear no argument]
@invites complaint
the other realms got the pretty zones and we got the rain, typical
[why is it|how is it] always [raining|foggy] in albion, [i rust just looking at it|my armor squeaks|my cloak never dries]
[too many|so many] [infiltrators|scouts] in this realm, [nobody|not one of them] wants to [heal|play a cleric]
@invites

