# ---------------- Albion: classes ----------------
@topic classes
@class Armsman
an armsman's job is simple. stand in front, hit hard, dont fall down
[every|one more] [day|fight] in [this|my] plate and i [creak|clank] like an old gate
@class Paladin
holding chants for an hour straight is a real skill, nobody believes me
[a paladin|my paladin] [never runs|does not run], [he walks with purpose|we just retreat with dignity|he holds the line]
@class Cleric
[heh, |]cleric life: [everyone loves you|you are everyone's best friend] [right up until|until] they die
smite cleric or rez cleric, the group always wants the other one
@class Friar
a friar does not need plate, a friar needs faith and a good staff
[i love being a friar|friar life is great], [robes|sandals] and a stick and [nobody expects a thing|i would not trade it]
@class Wizard
nothing in the realm hits like a wizard with a full power bar
the academy taught me fire and ice and very little about running
@class Theurgist
theurgist life, three pets out and none of them listen
@class Sorcerer
a sorcerer in a good group is a mez machine, the hibs hate it
@class Cabalist
cabalist pets are not ugly, they have character
@class Necromancer
[heh, |]being a [necro|necromancer] means half the realm [thinks i am|treats me like] a monster
@class Infiltrator
infiltrator life, nobody sees you and nobody thanks you
@class Scout
[an albion longbow|a good longbow] [sings|hums] when you let it go, [no other realm has that|hib bows sound like twigs]
@class Minstrel
minstrels carry this realm on speed songs and charm
@class Reaver
the church still asks about my flail. i do not answer
@class Mercenary
merc means i fight for albion and for the loot, mostly albion
@class Cleric,Friar
[healing albs|keeping albs alive] is [a calling|thankless work|the best job in the realm], [nobody|no one] [says thanks|says sorry] after a bad pull
@class Wizard,Theurgist,Sorcerer,Cabalist,Necromancer
the academy and the guilds argue, but every alb caster agrees the hibs are worse
@class Armsman,Paladin
[nothing|no feeling] beats [fresh polish on|a new strap on] my plate before a long hunt
@class

